"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Associated with rail lines.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":504.0,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":268.6666666666667,"r":382.0,"t":514.6666666666667},"charspan":[0,27],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/3","text":"Associated with rail lines."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Yarmouth County, northeastward to the Northumberland Strait.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":457.3333333333333,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":267.3333333333333,"r":527.3333333333334,"t":484.6666666666667},"charspan":[0,60],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/4","text":"Yarmouth County, northeastward to the Northumberland Strait."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"NS to ON and MI, south to IL and VA; AZ and NM. Introduced to NS.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":411.3333333333333,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":268.0,"r":489.0,"t":438.3333333333333},"charspan":[0,65],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/5","text":"NS to ON and MI, south to IL and VA; AZ and NM. Introduced to NS."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"caption","orig":"Photo by Sean Blaney","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":497.0,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":119.0,"r":199.66666666666666,"t":509.0},"charspan":[0,20],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/6","text":"Photo by Sean Blaney"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Chamaesyce vermiculata","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/1"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":477.3333333333333,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":82.33333333333333,"r":191.33333333333334,"t":487.6666666666667},"charspan":[0,22],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/7","text":"Chamaesyce vermiculata"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"section_header","level":1,"orig":"spurges","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":294.3333333333333,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":70.33333333333333,"r":119.0,"t":309.0},"charspan":[0,7],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/8","text":"spurges"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"These species are cosmopolitan; totalling 1500 species. As with Chamaesyce; they are typified by the very small unisexual flowers. Each pistillate flower bears a single pistil and is surrounded by several staminate flowers, each with a single stamen. All flowers are inserted into a lobed and glandular involucre forming a cyathium; functionally imitating a single flower a character unique to this family. Ovary has three locules, ovules and styles. Schizocarp is three-lobed. Plants contain a very bitter latex.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":200.66666666666663,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":70.33333333333333,"r":533.3333333333334,"t":278.0},"charspan":[0,513],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/9","text":"These species are cosmopolitan; totalling 1500 species. As with Chamaesyce; they are typified by the very small unisexual flowers. Each pistillate flower bears a single pistil and is surrounded by several staminate flowers, each with a single stamen. All flowers are inserted into a lobed and glandular involucre forming a cyathium; functionally imitating a single flower a character unique to this family. Ovary has three locules, ovules and styles. Schizocarp is three-lobed. Plants contain a very bitter latex."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"to species Page 549","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":169.66666666666663,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":89.0,"r":137.0,"t":182.33333333333337},"charspan":[0,10],"page_no":1},{"bbox":{"b":635.0,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":545.3333333333334,"r":596.6666666666666,"t":649.0},"charspan":[11,19],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/10","text":"to species Page 549"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"furniture","label":"page_footer","orig":"3-38 Euphorbiaceae","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":46.33333333333337,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":